Further to the below, I have now re-written the section at the end on ATE. It ultimately flags the same risks of not obtaining ‘full’ cover, and identifies that as the safest approach if the aim is to avoid an application, but
 also recognises the reasons why many firms may not want to go down that route, and notes the approach which PG/LD have taken (as I understand it – but please check what I say at the end of [47] in particular to make sure I have got that correct).

&nbsp;

Hopefully, that solves the difficulty and gives all cohorts the ability to make their own decisions based on their own circumstances (which will vary now more than ever, given that in previous phases most cohorts will have needed
 ‘full’ cover for the Cs own purposes in any event). And I expect, given the deadline for confirming positions is this Friday, most firms will have their plan in place already anyway. I’m keen not to have the ATE/security aspect take over the note which is
 really just meant to be about how the budgets work, hence why I have slightly tried to pull it back to that at the end.

&nbsp;

Anyway – if PD/LG are happy with the attached, it is ready for distribution. If there are further aspects which anyone would like to discuss, feel free to send them via email or call, I will be around this afternoon to assist
 if needed.

&nbsp;

Thanks

