nt or payment, there will need to be a holdback of funds by PG, sufficient to cover the outstanding limit on Toremis policies at the time that the settlement funds are received by PG. Those funds should then be held until the Toremis policies come off risk (which, given the stage of the proceedings, should occur within a short period of time).&nbsp;Can PG confirm that this is agreed in principle, subject to addressing the wording to achieve this?”&nbsp;We expect them to seek wording that is similar to the mechanism in clause 1(b) of the BHP 4th excess reimbursement deed. It will be difficult to justify a circumstance where it has been given in relation to the BHP 4th excess reimbursement deed but not for Toremis’ proposal, where the intention behind both structures is the same.&nbsp;Could you please confirm that this works? In the meantime, we asked if they could agree in principle to cap the amount to be provisioned/ring fenced by PG, as we have both in the wrapper deed and in clause 1(b) of the 4th layer reimbursement deed. &nbsp;We appreciate your prompt attention to this matter, given the time constraints.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 11 November 2025 15:22To: Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;Cc: James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;Thanks Nick &nbsp;Just sent the invite&nbsp;Tom&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From: Nick Paolazzi &lt