Morning Anna,
&nbsp;
Just following up on the below. With the good news that PG's application to resign as Lead Solicitor having been put on ice
 (pending further clarification from Pogust Goodhead or approval of the proposed agency relationship by the SRA), we need to consider the implications of this ruling.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Notwithstanding the case leads concerns over the AA, given the firm's intention that this AA arrangement was to create a firebreak
 between the Case Leads and the potential of interference from Gramercy, that we remain as lead Solicitor, we consider that this creates arguably an even bigger need for there to be clear daylight between the case leads and such potential interference. If there
 is a fear of funder interference, then this is even more acute in circumstances where we hold the role of Lead Solicitor, as opposed to that of another Claimant Firm, not&nbsp;least&nbsp;(as we have said before) because we owe duties to all clients, not just those of
 PG. Can you please give us your / the board's opinion on next steps?
&nbsp;
Pending the response to this, some of the below issues (re staff alienation etc) may become live again, especially the questions
 at the foot of the email - some of which require&nbsp;answers&nbsp;in any event. We &nbsp;also need to know whether the firm is intending on providing the Court with further information (if so, it should be made clear that the Case Leads, while intent on finding a solution,
 had the AA executed over their heads) or whether they intend to seek SRA approval of the AA (again making clear the Case Leads concerns).&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We have also become aware of a letter from Slaughter and May regarding litigation conduct and that this may have in turn resulted
 in or precipitated resignations from others in the business. If there are such concerns that have been raised regarding litigation conduct in the firm, that we are all senior employees of, then we need to know and we need to know what the position of the firm
 is. In case it was not obvious, each of us are considering our own regulatory position and whether we need to self report to the SRA and having this information will assist us in assessing this.
&nbsp;
Thanks,
&nbsp;
Case Leads

&nbsp;

































​​​​


































Michael&nbsp;Burke










(He/Him)
















