under clause 8.&nbsp; The Agency Agreement will enable PG to continue working on the liability trial and quantum workstream while you remain with us working your notice period -
this agreement&nbsp;is intended to ensure that strategic control of the Lead cases does not rest with me/Alicia to alleviate the misguided allegations of champerty. Albeit I will continue to have strategic input and meaningful involvement.
 It is a pragmatic solution to the allegations.



Whilst LD will retain the title of sole Lead Solicitor, this will not practically change
much day to day.&nbsp; LD will be required to consult with us in connection with decisions and we expect matters to continue in the manner they have to date -&nbsp;your working relationships with LD will
 be unchanged in that regard. Structurally and to secure PG’s continued involvement in the cases, PG employees will be delegated work by Leigh Day. As you know, PG and LD have been working together for years, including on behalf of many other solicitor
 firms, and&nbsp;this Agency Agreement will mean that PG to will continue doing so whilst not retaining the title of Lead Solicitor.&nbsp;



For the avoidance of doubt, there will be no change to your employment contract and Leigh Day do not and will have no employer-employee relationship with you.&nbsp; In the circumstances consent by employees is not necessary for PG to execute the agency agreement,
 as this is a structural rather than substantive change it should not be an issue.
As continuing PG employees you will continue to work on the Non-Common Work streams as required and directed solely by PG (which includes matters related to the non-Lead Cases, which are
 not subject to the Agency Agreement).&nbsp;If you have any regulatory concerns that you wish to inform the clients of, please do let us know specifically what they are.
In addition we are now interviewing so with time this work-stream will be gradually handed over - in a sensible way that serves our clients' best interests.&nbsp;
We, LD and counsel have approved this solution which adheres with and is entirely consistent with the existing legal framework, offering the best path forward in the best interests of our clients. We also welcome
 any specific input you may wish to contribute.&nbsp;
As to your future employment, as we have previously explained, you are obliged to work until end of your notice period, in accordance with the terms of your contract.&nbsp; Once your notice period has expired, you
 will be free to commence working for Johnson Law Group, together with Peter Gallagher, should you so choose.&nbsp; In this specific and limited regard, your covenants will not be enforced.
Finally, the firm is very mindful of its professional and regulatory responsibilities and would never expect you to do anything to compromise those. The firm will always supervise its lawyers and safeguard them
 from potential breaches, and we trust you will do so at all times too, both on your own behalf and on behalf of those you supervise. We do not intend doing anything, nor have we done anything, that would put us or you in breach of any regulatory or professional
 requirements which remain an absolute priority to us. Everything we have done or are intending to do is with the best interests of our clients as well as our staff in mind first and foremost.
Separately, a reminder that the updates to the PG claimants’ committees have not yet gone out.&nbsp; If you have not sent them out by midday tomorrow, our duty to the clients will require me and Alicia to communicate
 with the committees directly.
We very much hope that this email can now draw these discussions to a conclusion so that we all focus on the imminent trial and delivering the best results to our clients.
Best, Anna
