 forward in the best interests of our clients. We also welcome any specific input you may wish to contribute.&nbsp;
As to your future employment, as we have previously explained, you are obliged to work until end of your notice period, in accordance with the terms of
 your contract.&nbsp; Once your notice period has expired, you will be free to commence working for Johnson Law Group, together with Peter Gallagher, should you so choose.&nbsp; In this specific and limited regard, your covenants will not be enforced.
Finally, the firm is very mindful of its professional and regulatory responsibilities and would never expect you to do anything to compromise those. The
 firm will always supervise its lawyers and safeguard them from potential breaches, and we trust you will do so at all times too, both on your own behalf and on behalf of those you supervise. We do not intend doing anything, nor have we done anything, that
 would put us or you in breach of any regulatory or professional requirements which remain an absolute priority to us. Everything we have done or are intending to do is with the best interests of our clients as well as our staff in mind first and foremost.
We very much hope that this email can now draw these discussions to a conclusion so that we all focus on the imminent trial and delivering the best results
 to our clients.
